invariant: INV-22
file: srv_handshake.c
catches: test/e2e.sh
builds: bin/recclient bin/tlsclient bin/tlsclient_ecdsa bin/tlsclient_ca bin/tlsclient_ca_ecdsa bin/tlsclient_webpki bin/tlsclient_webpki_aes bin/tlsclient_pq bin/example_psk bin/example_pinned bin/example_ca bin/example_webpki bin/pemkey bin/pemkey_ecdsa bin/tlsserver
reason: the blocking server sends its Certificate and CertificateVerify on
  a handshake a ticket authenticated. No in-process test drives
  srv_handshake.c, because both of its ends block on a socket, so the e2e
  legs against bin/tlsserver are what hold it: OpenSSL's s_client and this
  tree's pinned client each resume a ticket, and a resumed hello that meets
  a Certificate fails the handshake.

